# Not published, and not needed at runtime.
#
# These were previously hidden by a `routes` rule in vercel.json, which had to go: the legacy
# `routes` array suppresses the modern `headers` property, so the site sent no security headers
# at all. Excluding the files from the upload is stronger anyway — a file that was never
# deployed cannot be served by a rule someone deletes later.
#
# ⚠ DO NOT add `lib/` here. Those modules are imported at runtime by api/*.mjs; excluding them
#   breaks every serverless function on the site.
tools/
blog-src/
partials/
